"M. Cao" <mcao@u.washington.edu> writes:

> My digital unix 4.0D had a external disk, that needs to move to Tru64
> system. How can I move a AdvFS on the external disk to another system ?

Write down the output concerning your disk from

/etc/fdmns # ls -lR [my_domain]

It may look something like this:
/etc/fdmns# ls -lR work_domain
total 0
lrwxr-xr-x   1 root     system         9 May 26  1997 rz0c -> /dev/rz0c

Take down the machine and remove the disk, connect it to the new one
with suitable scsi-id and restore the subdirectory and link(s) on the
other machine.

Kjell



