   the "To," "Cc," and "Newsgroups" headers for details. ]]

In article
<Pine.A41.4.10.10003091315550.148416-100000@homer10.u.washington.edu>,
M. Cao <mcao@u.washington.edu> wrote:

>My digital unix 4.0D had a external disk, that needs to move to Tru64
>system. How can I move a AdvFS on the external disk to another system ?

Move the disk to the new system.

Run the /sbin/advfs/advscan command (man advscan).  Something like

        /sbin/advfs/advscan -r rzXX     

where rzXX is the location of the disk on the new system.

Then go to /etc/fdmns and you should see new directories with names
like:

        domain_rzXXa
        domain_rzXXg
or
        domain_rzXXc

or similar.  These are the domains that were found on the disk.

The domain name is just the name of the directory in /etc/fdmns, so you
can use the 'mv' command to rename the /etc/fdmns/domain_rzXXx
directory to whatever you want to call the domain.



