1. If you want to on-line to add one new disk, before you plug-in the disk,
you type the following command: scu show edt, then plug it, type scu scan
edt , then scu show edt again you will see the new disk id.
2. Make sure which one is your new disk. then create the special file(or you
can reboot your system, system will create it for u). like following(suppose
your new disk is on BUS 2 SCSI ID:4 the device name should be 8*2+4=20 ->
rz20):
cd /dev
./MAKEDEV rz20
then partition using disklabel:
disklabel -rw /dev/rrz20a rzxx
disklabel -e rz20
then edit the partition table(a to h). Please reference the man page.
if u want to create advfs, using
mkfset /dev/rz20? <domain-name> (where > ? is the partition you partitioned)
mkfset <domain-name> <fileset-name>
mount <domain-name>#<fileset-name> <mount-point>
if u want to create UFS, using newfs command.

Rest Regards,
Allen Hung


