Holger van Koll (holger.vankoll@swisscom.com) wrote:
: If I configure my interface at boot time with

: ifconfig tu0 ip1 netmask-for1 alias ip2

: it sets the broadcast-address to that for ip2. Thats why I want to create a
: 2nd interface.

Yes. Just set the broadcast address explicitly, using 'broadcast addr' keyword.
Do not forget to specify the class of the alias address (using /CIDR notation)
as well ...

If you absolutely need to have a second interface, you can always fake it
with a slip interface which does not connect to anything.

/Serge.P

