Which version of cluster are you trying this on. V5.0 has a feature that
enable this but for the older versions the outgoing address is the
primary address for that connection (ie if the network cards primary
address is 192.168.1.1 and the virtual address is 192.168.1.50, the
remote machine will see the connection coming from 192.168.1.1). For
intra cluster comms you should use memeory channel (if you have it - it
is required by the way for V5.0)

/WB/

